cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Disper26, please cite the software version you used using the
  metadata below. Please also cite the accompanying paper when it is available.
type: software
title: Disper26
version: 0.1.105
date-released: 2026-11-26
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24566846
repository-code: "https://github.com/qnishida/Disper26"
authors:
  - family-names: Nishida
    given-names: Kiwamu
abstract: >-
  Disper26 computes Rayleigh and Love surface-wave dispersion in isotropic and
  vertically transversely isotropic layered media. It provides C++, C, Fortran
  and Python interfaces, automatic-differentiation kernels and phase-velocity
  Hessians, and Romberg refinement for gradient models.
keywords:
  - surface waves
  - seismic dispersion
  - transverse isotropy
  - automatic differentiation
  - sensitivity kernels
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
